{"title":"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 49","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_but_very_similar_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative but very similar Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(best_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (best solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Super_fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Super fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d737a4088cc4d9061c296f96c1fa7232d8d8d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(27); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(10pt)); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,X,Y,Z; A=(3,3); B=(0,0); C=(6,0); D=(4,0); E=(4,2); F=(1,1); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(B--E); draw(C--F); X=intersectionpoint(A--D,C--F); Y=intersectionpoint(B--E,A--D); Z=intersectionpoint(B--E,C--F); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,NW); label(&quot;$N_1$&quot;,X,NE); label(&quot;$N_2$&quot;,Y,WNW); label(&quot;$N_3$&quot;,Z,S); [/asy]\" width=\"308\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p>In the figure, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aa4ad1cf6a0ad719767e1739c9b689debc60142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> are one-third of their respective sides. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac73af1f6e9bf570ca0661c05b2a7ee606ff333d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AN_2}: \\overline{N_2N_1}: \\overline{N_1D} = 3: 3: 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"21\" />, and similarly for lines BE and CF. Then the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341f10139964e36c80c502896315051f9dada0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1N_2N_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fc86bce9ddae7ef321e3e5fbaa960e2184a060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } \\frac {1}{10} \\triangle ABC \\qquad \\text{(B) } \\frac {1}{9} \\triangle ABC \\qquad \\text{(C) } \\frac{1}{7}\\triangle ABC\\qquad \\text{(D) } \\frac{1}{6}\\triangle ABC\\qquad \\text{(E) } \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"677\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e738c48637c47390c23286b610b73960085a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac104c6caa87e996640eea068cd1f060741d9354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADC] = \\frac{1}{3}K,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623ea3f8c8c823a374525c05aca4eff0ba57355c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1DC] = \\frac{1}{7} [ADC] = \\frac{1}{21}K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0ab25b29983dd61c9c4683601e8856a46a5765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_2EA]=[N_3FB] = \\frac{1}{21}K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"211\" height=\"37\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/6/10655cbdf9b963a63b4d060903ab43315d1cfdf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_2N_1CE] = [ADC] - [N_1DC]-[N_2EA] = \\frac{5}{21}K,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"397\" height=\"38\" /> and same for the other quadrilaterals. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff8e43b91d4e5d54ac467cec54705a555c8892a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33cc80fa8f093e155c5be46d2e5d9da3d7e1ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> minus all the other regions we just computed. That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616c520b2e2f0684b7781573805e32a2d9ffbd97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[N_1N_2N_3] = K - 3\\left(\\frac{1}{21}K\\right) - 3\\left(\\frac{5}{21}\\right)K = K - \\frac{6}{7}K = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{7}[ABC]}\\]\" width=\"522\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_but_very_similar_Solution\">Alternative but very similar Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative but very similar Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e738c48637c47390c23286b610b73960085a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac104c6caa87e996640eea068cd1f060741d9354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADC] = \\frac{1}{3}K,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623ea3f8c8c823a374525c05aca4eff0ba57355c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1DC] = \\frac{1}{7} [ADC] = \\frac{1}{21}K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37fce5288f67751dd3f6a152e8e4b14cbf345258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_2EA]=[N_3FB]=[N_1DC] = \\frac{1}{21}K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"297\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729cf20d5d565a67764306096056467fc8055a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADC]+[BEA]+[CFB]=\\frac{1}{3}K+\\frac{1}{3}K+\\frac{1}{3}K = K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"406\" height=\"37\" /> Then we can implement a similar but different area addition postulate to the first solution. It will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15d341fffdf0b808eca38f9b014d34e4e173fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADC]+[BEA]+[CFB]=K-\\frac{1}{21}K-\\frac{1}{21}K-\\frac{1}{21}K+[N_1N_2N_3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"525\" height=\"37\" /> (PIE in action). Using transitive property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22dcf0258809e18635241867014cd87a039347b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K-\\frac{1}{21}K-\\frac{1}{21}K-\\frac{1}{21}K+[N_1N_2N_3] = K.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"342\" height=\"37\" /> Subtracting and adding on both sides gives: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d5583b8b79db376233a52eb25afb0aba84f61e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[N_1N_2N_3] = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{7}[ABC]}\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"48\" /> ~many credits to the first solution ~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28best_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(best_solution)\">Solution 2 (best solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (best solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can force this triangle to be equilateral because the ratios are always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1b281c81f3a98f7b343090012b984eea1a1b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> no matter which rotation, and with the symmetry of the equilateral triangle, it is safe to assume that this may be the truth (symmetry is very important, kids). Then, we can do a simple coordinate bash. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44ec7c8483beb0b557c6b050f885200aba66e8db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,3\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc97d11165519987d52074b4f215a0f9837b9b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. We then create a new point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> at the center of everything. It should be noted because of similarity between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c96b81550d3455e18f5bbbaa5a1dee4932b12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle N_{1}N_{2}N_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we can find the scale factor between the two triangle by simply dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5c1fbf3deb5eeac634e1f78ecd81803e9e7f05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_{2}O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" />(not nitrous oxide) by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c53cc93aa43cc55bea0dc2511833fe6bdda020f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. First, we need to find the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedf94ab09f078974884f0cab20c6d145e045a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is easily found at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/713694fd570d2b15428b2e049409a94fb16cc0d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedf94ab09f078974884f0cab20c6d145e045a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> be found by calculating equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e46e6c91a27e1d9a70a32cc4b6b4ed32260ef889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,2\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63f8f64f9c3fbdc38ca2b60a5354101380d9c05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{x\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"41\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86f58cb609fa753024f1173510c877971f8e4e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65ad5265be7f178a4c9fceb91277e3475b92f430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />. We see that they be at the same <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-value. Quick maths calculate the x value to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/5466c0d6e6f2cb903801f0909901ed04700abad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"111\" height=\"50\" /> which be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc71f3d56c74c0f7c2026d743ee6ac7eb9dda081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\frac{3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Another quick maths caculation of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-value lead it be equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc797e28967dccf0d1c368f67d2c7dd476ee3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}*\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+3\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"133\" height=\"53\" /> which be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa5e02d1d651f35f23954a15cbe5c4b55f0f06a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"37\" />. Peferct, so now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aedf94ab09f078974884f0cab20c6d145e045a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3423aecc1af1bf297b20f542d4c390ad2eff2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3\\frac{3}{7},1\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" />. Subtracting this coordinate with the coordinates of the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> give you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8145ed9816e28dd03c94ec57a1be0dcb48a2914d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />. Pythagorean theorem on that gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311156930a9e64e6d32cdb056381b42c88c00d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{84}}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc1e6fdcf758f5ada560be67699873113f834ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"41\" height=\"45\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is vertically above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> units. The scale factor is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca75236e924ef087b307e3a01aaa2dff47b2bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" /> giving us an answer of: ~Lopkiloinm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbca2f13b771e172a4d8632055d9f05776bbb211.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{7}[ABC]}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" /> (Note: the presence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the denominator gives hints on the answer, so when you see it, 1/7 looks like the obvious choice) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n(Another note: the question gives you the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1b281c81f3a98f7b343090012b984eea1a1b04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> so I did not need to use that many steps to calculate the coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e715db9bdeefe6c4f6b079451b994061a92e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, directly attaining it to be at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3423aecc1af1bf297b20f542d4c390ad2eff2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3\\frac{3}{7},1\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" /> After realizing this, this method should actually be pretty quick, may even be quicker than the non coordinate method. Regardless, if you don't get the ratio and you encounter a problem similar to this, the coordinate bash with all these calculations should get you the correct answer. Also, there is an even bashier way using all the points and shoelace formula. That takes too much time.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Visual graphical proof.\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-seventh_area_triangle#/media/File%3ATriangleOneSeventhAreaGraphicalSoln.png\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-seventh_area_triangle#/media/File%3ATriangleOneSeventhAreaGraphicalSoln.png</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using Routh's Theorem\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb16bda17327c3d81cb46349b1a8c18123b73893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{BD}{CD} = \\frac{\\frac{2BC}{3}}{\\frac{BC}{3}} = \\frac{2}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"168\" height=\"50\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b0046a7446d1f3047baf2c28fd25355f57ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366f63e900afa56359ef3f7da33ae2f027b8d168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3] = [ABC]\\cdot\\frac{(xyz-1)^2}{(xy+y+1)(yz+z+1)(zx+x+1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"463\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a031e5838fa707d6c54e80cbf3f981cdc8bb9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/e/b7edad0dee89c53b439ba6bb17f8eb2806956b9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3] = [ABC]\\cdot\\frac{7^2}{7^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff038d40a36c04eb9f19ae71d224e1d20dbfc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3] = [ABC]\\cdot\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore the answer is,\n</p><p>(C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab2751968e25272aedf5fed31fac7f0124c0457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3] = \\frac{[ABC]}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Super_fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Super_fast)\">Solution 5 (Super fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Super fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use triangle area ratios. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4af57e01c35fab7af6b548f34695722f59a787d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3]=[ABD]-[BFN_3]-[N_3N_2AF]-[N_3N_1DB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"451\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>So let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece24a6edfd55801692b4abdde1d0e962f918050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807a1d8d0c7fc7db5fd021348d4b7ff76f5ca0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABD]=\\frac{2}{3}S, [ADC]=\\frac{1}{3}S, [N_1DC]=\\frac{1}{21}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"343\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a81203eb3e5b737923060b3aebf7ed5dca6c5ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FBC]=\\frac{1}{3}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86aa19d5b2794787ae64965332288c370da61297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FBDN_1]=\\frac{6}{21}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, we can use this argument to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b2c8a6ce1a83394b7a0621edb3412422c44790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABE]=\\frac{1}{3}S, [FBN_3]=\\frac{1}{21}S, [AN_2E]=\\frac{1}{21}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"357\" height=\"38\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/3/d636a73d1cb9d44e66bf57c5cac7dfb20cfe803f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[FN_3N_2A]=\\frac{5}{21}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77bea3739522d7fc7c0e5ae9ee95c32854cd088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3]=\\frac{2}{3}S-\\frac{5}{21}S-\\frac{6}{21}S=\\frac{1}{7}S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"290\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>So therefore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/74690a513e1091a57f441c1952c69fed2ff40c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3]=\\frac{1}{7}[ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"38\" />, select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>You can also use a similar idea (Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion) to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff8e43b91d4e5d54ac467cec54705a555c8892a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[N_1N_2N_3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. Notice that the triangle we desire is the intersection set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3165e9cfff2f7762654b325066f73b1ad2670963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AFC}, \\triangle{ABD}, \\triangle{BEC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" />. So we just PIE it out.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME\" title=\"1952 AHSME\">1952 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1952 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1952\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 48\">Problem 48</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 50\">Problem 50</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1